Required behaviour.
(a) Files. core-lines.json may hold `storage` {scratch_roots: [<dir>], scratch_exclude: [<path>]}, read on every request like the ranges. Each top-level entry of a root is one of:
- owned: its `.spawn-owner` file, "<pid> <start ticks>" (the pid file's form), names a process that still runs at that start time; or, with no marker, something in it changed in the last 24 h;
- gone: its marker names a process that does not run, or a pid now used by another process (other start ticks);
- idle: no marker, and nothing in it changed in 24 h.
Gone and idle are "nobody owns", kept apart by their reason. Never counted, whatever the configuration says:
- symlinks, never followed at any depth;
- an entry holding any *.jsonl file (a transcript tree);
- `.transcripts`, names starting `incident-`, names ending `.pending` or `-pending`;
- /data/recovery, /var/backups/spawn-sessions and the Claude Code projects directory (and anything under them), should a root ever take them in;
